tmux cheatsheet
===============

C-Space is this setup's prefix. Press it, then the next key.
C- means Ctrl; M- means Alt. Uppercase means Shift plus that letter.
h/j/k/l move left/down/up/right. "cfg" marks custom bindings.


Sessions
--------

From a shell:

  KEY / COMMAND                ACTION
  --------------------------  ----------------------------
  tmux new -s work             Start named session
  tmux new -As work            Attach or create session
  tmux ls                      List sessions
  tmux attach -t work          Attach to session
  tmux kill-session -t NAME    End named session

Inside tmux:

  KEY / COMMAND                ACTION
  --------------------------  ----------------------------
  C-Space, then d              Detach; leave session running
  C-Space, then $              Rename current session
  C-Space, then w              Browse sessions and windows


Windows
-------

  KEY / COMMAND                ACTION
  --------------------------  ----------------------------
  C-Space, then c              Create a window
  C-Space, then n              Next window
  C-Space, then M-p            Previous window
  C-Space, then ,              Rename current window
  C-Space, then &              Close window (confirm)


Panes
-----

  KEY / COMMAND                ACTION
  --------------------------  ----------------------------
  C-Space, then v              Split side by side (cfg)
  C-Space, then s              Split top/bottom (cfg)
  C-Space, then %              Split side by side (default)
  C-Space, then "              Split top/bottom (default)
  C-Space, then h/j/k/l        Move between panes (cfg)
  C-Space, then Arrow          Move between panes (default)
  C-Space, then H/J/K/L        Resize 5 cells (cfg)
  C-Space, then C-Arrow        Resize 1 cell (default)
  C-Space, then o              Cycle to next pane
  C-Space, then z              Zoom or restore pane
  C-Space, then x              Close pane (confirm)

Repeat H/J/K/L quickly to continue resizing.


Copy mode
---------

  KEY / COMMAND                ACTION
  --------------------------  ----------------------------
  C-Space, then Esc            Enter copy mode (cfg)
  C-Space, then [              Enter copy mode (default)
  v                            Select characters
  C-v                          Toggle rectangular selection
  y                            Copy selection and exit
  H / L                        Jump to line start/end
  / and ?                      Search forward/backward
  n / N                        Repeat search forward/back
  Esc                          Cancel copy mode
  C-Space, then p              Paste buffer (cfg)
  C-Space, then ]              Paste buffer (default)


Configuration and help
-----------------------

  KEY / COMMAND                ACTION
  --------------------------  ----------------------------
  C-Space, then r              Reload this config
  C-Space, then :              Open command prompt
  :cheatsheet                  Open cheatsheet popup
  C-Space, then ?              List key bindings

Load the config from a pane or outside tmux:

  tmux source-file ~/.config/tmux/tmux.conf


Notes
-----

This config replaces the default C-b prefix with C-Space.
It rebinds p to paste; use C-Space, then M-p for the previous window.
It rebinds s to split panes; use C-Space, then w to browse sessions/windows.
Mouse is on; windows and panes start numbering at 1.
